{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall place the cover upon the ark from above.</b> And afterward, 'And into the ark you shall place the testimony.' How so? From the month of Av going in reverse, the tablets were resting in the ark that Moses made, as it is written in the portion of Ekev: 'And I shall make an ark of shittim wood, and I shall hew two tablets of stone,' etc. And on the 25th of Kislev, which immediately follows, when the Tabernacle and all its furnishings were finished, then they first placed the cover upon the ark, while the tablets were still in the ark that Moses made, until the first of Nisan, when the Tabernacle and all its furnishings were anointed, and he lifted the cover and placed the tablets in the ark that Bezalel made. And that is what is said: 'And into the ark you shall place the testimony.'\nAnd according to its plain sense: 'And into <b>the ark</b>' — it will already have been placed <b>et the testimony</b>; afterward <b>and you shall place the cover.</b> And since it took up the subject and proceeded with the making of the cover, it wrote for you first, 'and you shall place the cover,' in order to finish all the acts of making incumbent upon it." "<b>And into the ark you shall place the testimony.</b> Here it commands to place the tablets in the ark, and above where it is written 'and you shall place into the ark,' it gives the reason that it shall not be removed from it." "<b>Which I shall give you.</b> These are the second tablets, for this passage was said in the forty days, the last ones, and the first ones were broken on the 17th of Tammuz that passed." "<b>[And into the ark.</b> In the ark.]"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בעשיית הכפרת' — 'the making of the cover' — appears to have a feminine singular suffix ('incumbent upon it'), which is difficult; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:29.858370493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}